Write up for Team Project 1

  So for the first team project, Cody and I decided to make a game call Stone Bridge Escapade. The concept is rather simple. The king of the land is looking for a suitor for the
princess and so you (the player) have to collect 4 treasures to make yourself worthy in the eyes of the king for his daughter's hand. But there are other suitors that will harm 
you if you get close to them since they also want the princess's hand. You win once you collect all 4 treasures.

In terms of my contribution to the project, I designed the sprites for the 4 treasure, the backgrounds for starting screen, the intro screen, the gameplay scene, game over scene, 
and the victory scene. And I also picked out the background music. Cody was in charge of designing the player and enemy sprite. In terms of the coding part we evenly split the 
scenes where we wrote code/fix each other's code for the scenes ranging from gameplay to each item, to the enemy scene. We also collaborated together on the global.gd with cody 
creating it and me implementing it so that it runs on the game itself. 
